      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1881 the Northern Pacific Railroad was approaching the river confluence that would become the heart of Potomac.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://montanahistoriclandscape.com/tag/potomac-montana/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Potomac served as a vital supply point for miners, lumberjacks, and ranchers during the early days of the region.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
